Initial review runner failed the post-Enter URL assertion: wait_for_load_state(load) can observe the already-loaded source page before keyboard-triggered navigation begins. Production click path and keyboard focus assertion had passed. Replace with URL-specific navigation wait and rerun; no production change.
Second attempt reached a reload text-equality assertion before final results were saved. Added click expect_navigation(load) and diagnostic details to distinguish stale document sampling from a production text mismatch.
Diagnostic rerun resolved the second failure: Firefox primary /NEPL3/docs/spec/00-contract.html reload returned HTTP 304 with identical text. The failed conjunct was the overly strict status==200, not content equality. Accept valid cache revalidation 200/304 while still requiring exact article text.
Fourth attempt: primary Chromium and Firefox completed, then first-Tab link/focus assertion failed in WebKit. Preserve observed focus in final results and independently verify keyboard Enter activation with explicit locator focus in all engines; do not equate this to successful WebKit Tab traversal.
Fifth attempt: immediate post-load fragment scroll assertion observed zero before deferred layout/anchor positioning. Replaced immediate sampling by bounded wait_for_function(scrollY>0), preserving real fragment positioning requirement.
Sixth attempt: WebKit immediate fragment reload wait timed out after 30s. Independent isolated WebKit probe (JS on/off, load/networkidle) passed initial positioning and reload in all four cases. Journey now waits for initial fragment position and resource idle before triggering reload, then verifies final position.
